---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Contribute | Fireside Library" activeNav="contribute">

<section class="pt-24 pb-12">
  <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-6 md:px-12">
    <div class="max-w-3xl">
      <p class="text-[0.8125rem] text-gray-500 mb-6">A note for anyone thinking about pitching in</p>
      <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-black tracking-tight leading-[1.15] mb-4">We could really use your help, and we'll be honest about what that looks like.</h1>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="pb-16">
  <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-6 md:px-12">
    <div class="max-w-3xl text-[1.0625rem] leading-[1.8] text-gray-800 space-y-6">

    <p>Right now we are a small group of Baha'is — mostly in Boston, a few elsewhere — who write, edit, and host these firesides. We are not a nonprofit. We are not commissioned by anyone. We do this on weekends and in the margins of the day.</p>

    <p>The honest version of what we need is below. Pick whatever fits your life. None of it requires us interviewing you first.</p>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold tracking-tight pt-6 pb-1">The most useful thing you can do</h2>

    <p>Read a fireside. Try it with three or four friends. Tell us what worked and what didn't.</p>

    <p>We have plenty of words. What we lack is evidence about which words actually land in someone's living room. A short note describing how a conversation went — where the group spent the most time, where the silence felt awkward, what question someone asked that we didn't anticipate — is more valuable than almost anything else you could send us.</p>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold tracking-tight pt-6 pb-1">If you'd like to write</h2>

    <p>Some of the firesides are good. Some of them need to be rewritten. A couple are missing. We'd be glad of help with any of those.</p>

    <p>Writing a fireside is more work than it looks like. You start with source material, draft something, sit with it for a week, come back and realize half of it is wrong, rewrite. We use AI to help with first drafts; the rewrite has to come from a human voice. The full cycle — planning, draft, review, rewrite, beta, v1 — usually takes a couple of months.</p>

    <p>If that sounds like something you'd want to take on, open an issue with the topic you're thinking about, or email us. We'll pair you with an editor.</p>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold tracking-tight pt-6 pb-1">If you'd like to edit</h2>

    <p>This is where we are most short-handed. A good editor reads with a skeptical friend in mind: would they buy this? Would they feel preached at? Did the writer reach for a quote when they should have written a sentence? These are unglamorous questions; they are the ones that matter most.</p>

    <p>If you have edited writing before — anything, anywhere — we would love to hear from you.</p>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold tracking-tight pt-6 pb-1">What you should expect</h2>

    <p>Slow turnaround on reviews. Iteration on copy that you might have thought was done. Disagreement, occasionally, about what to keep. Mostly, though: gratitude. We are aware that anyone who shows up to do this work is doing us a favour.</p>

    <p>Everything lives on GitHub — drafts, source material, the editorial process. If that's an unfamiliar tool, we will help.</p>

    <div class="pt-6">
      <a href="https://github.com/naysawn/fireside-library" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 bg-gray-900 text-white font-semibold text-[0.9375rem] px-5 py-3 rounded-md no-underline hover:-translate-y-px transition">
        <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor"><path d="M12 0C5.37 0 0 5.37 0 12c0 5.31 3.435 9.795 8.205 11.385.6.105.825-.255.825-.57 0-.285-.015-1.23-.015-2.235-3.015.555-3.795-.735-4.035-1.41-.135-.345-.72-1.41-1.23-1.695-.42-.225-1.02-.78-.015-.795.945-.015 1.62.87 1.845 1.23 1.08 1.815 2.805 1.305 3.495.99.105-.78.42-1.305.765-1.605-2.67-.3-5.46-1.335-5.46-5.925 0-1.305.465-2.385 1.23-3.225-.12-.3-.54-1.53.12-3.18 0 0 1.005-.315 3.3 1.23.96-.27 1.98-.405 3-.405s2.04.135 3 .405c2.295-1.56 3.3-1.23 3.3-1.23.66 1.65.24 2.88.12 3.18.765.84 1.23 1.905 1.23 3.225 0 4.605-2.805 5.625-5.475 5.925.435.375.81 1.095.81 2.22 0 1.605-.015 2.895-.015 3.3 0 .315.225.69.825.57A12.02 12.02 0 0024 12c0-6.63-5.37-12-12-12z"/></svg>
        Find the project on GitHub
      </a>
    </div>

    <p class="text-gray-500 italic pt-8">Thanks for reading this far. Whatever you decide to do is fine — including nothing.</p>

    </div>
  </div>
</section>

</Layout>
